B4 (D070, the founder's approval of the conversion bug fixes B1-B7, 24 Nov 2026; action 2026-W48-B4, card K-170). Checkout code,
  signed off one by one. One property:
  - `keepalive: true` on `onPaid`'s `fetch("/api/preorder/confirm", ...)`, so the request survives the `location.assign("/thanks...")`
    that follows at once (it was cancelled on iOS: "TypeError: Load failed", and only the Razorpay webhook confirmed the order).
    Same method, headers and body; still not awaited; same order (events, confirm, navigate). The comment above the call says why.
  - The logic signature (checkout-signatures/...PreorderForm.tsx.json) gains exactly one line, `keepalive: true,`; nothing in `jsx`.
  - Proof: test/preorder-confirm-keepalive.test.tsx (a new file, because the frozen checkout tests take literal-only patches).

B3 (D070, the founder's approval of the conversion bug fixes B1-B7, 24 Nov 2026; action 2026-W48-B3, card K-171). Checkout code and
  a parent's details on their device, signed off one by one: per-tab sessionStorage, name/phone/email only, never the child's age,
  cleared on payment or after 30 minutes, no long-term storage. Three lines here, the rest in a new helper:
  - `import { clearFormDraft, useFormDraft } from "./form-draft";` and `const draftRef = useFormDraft();` (a ref callback: when the
    form appears it puts a saved draft back into the EMPTY name, phone and email fields, sets `.value` only, so no event, no
    `preorder_form_started`, no validation; and it saves each later change to those three fields through native input/change
    listeners on the form), with `ref={draftRef}` on the `<form>` (a `ref` is not part of the jsx signature).
  - `clearFormDraft();` in `onPaid`, right after `preorderAnalytics.purchase(...)` and before the confirm request and the move to
    /thanks. Closing the payment window (`onDismiss`) keeps the draft: "Your details are still here" stays true.
  - The helper is src/features/preorder/components/form-draft.ts (a new file: `src/features/preorder/lib/` is frozen and takes none).
    One key, `kh_preorder_draft`, `{ v: 1, savedAt, parentName, phone, email }`; a draft older than 30 minutes is deleted, not
    restored; every storage access is in a try/catch. It calls no tracker and sends nothing.
  - The logic signature (checkout-signatures/...PreorderForm.tsx.json) gains exactly three lines (the import, the `useFormDraft`
    declaration, the `clearFormDraft();` call); nothing in `jsx` changes.
  - Proof: test/preorder-form-draft.test.ts and test/preorder-form-draft-render.test.tsx (new files, because the frozen checkout
    tests take literal-only patches). Two test-isolation lines because jsdom's sessionStorage outlives a test: test/setup.ts clears
    it after every test, and test/guards/checkout-jsx-contract.test.tsx clears it at the start of each state it renders (no
    assertion, fixture or expectation changed; the frozen PreorderForm.test.tsx is untouched and green).

B7c (D070, the founder's approval of the conversion bug fixes B1-B7, 24 Nov 2026; action 2026-W48-B7c, card K-174). Measurement, signed
  off one by one: a signal for the parent who leaves the page with the payment sheet open. A watcher object, a ref and four calls here;
  the rest is in new files (src/lib/tracking/payment-window.ts, src/lib/tracking/beacon.ts):
  - `import { watchPaymentWindow, type PaymentWindowWatch } from "@/lib/tracking/payment-window";` and `useEffect` in the react import.
  - `const sheetWatch = useRef<PaymentWindowWatch | null>(null);` and `useEffect(() => () => sheetWatch.current?.close(), []);` (the
    listener goes if the form unmounts).
  - `const sheet = watchPaymentWindow(tier);` and `sheetWatch.current = sheet;` right before `startCheckout`, `if (opened) sheet.opened();`
    right after it (the sheet is up: from now the first `visibilitychange` to hidden sends `preorder_payment_window_hidden { tier }` once,
    at once, by beacon, to PostHog only), and `sheet.close();` as the first statement of `onDismiss` and of `onPaid` (stops listening).
  - Nothing else moves: `onDismiss` still calls `preorderAnalytics.dismissed(tier)` (so `preorder_dismissed` still fires, proved by
    test/preorder-payment-window.test.tsx), `onPaid` the same funnel call, the confirm request, the draft clear and the navigation, in
    the same order. No request, state, JSX or attribute changes. Frozen files (`analytics.ts`, `checkout.ts`, `posthog.ts`,
    `PostHogGate.tsx`, `proxy.ts`) are untouched.
  - The logic signature (checkout-signatures/...PreorderForm.tsx.json) gains exactly these lines: the react import now with `useEffect`,
    the `watchPaymentWindow` import, the `sheetWatch` ref and its effect, the `sheet` declaration and assignment, `sheet.close();` twice,
    and `if (opened) sheet.opened();`; nothing in `jsx`.
  - Proof: test/preorder-payment-window.test.tsx (a new file, because the frozen checkout tests take literal-only patches) and
    test/tracking-beacon.test.ts; registry rows in src/lib/tracking/events.ts (status added, D070) held to inventory §17.

B2 (D070, the founder's approval of the conversion bug fixes B1-B7, 24 Nov 2026, checkout code signed off one by one; action 2026-W48-B2,
  card K-172): a payment finished outside the page still reaches the address step. Additive; most of it is in new files
  (./pending-payment.ts, ./redirect-checkout.ts, ./PayRecoveryNotice.tsx, src/content/en-IN/store/pay-recovery.ts, the two routes under
  src/app/store/pay/, src/layouts/StoreShell/ThanksCleanup.client.tsx):
  - Imports: `normalisePhone` (from ../lib/validate), `clearPending`, `confirmThenGoToThanks`, `savePending`, `usePendingPayment`,
    `PayRecoveryNotice`, `payReturnUrl`, `prefersRedirectCheckout`.
  - `const recovery = usePendingPayment(tier, () => setState("idle"));` asks the server ONCE on arrival about the order this tab started
    (paid: /thanks; open: the notice; anything else: nothing) and again when the page is restored from the back-forward cache.
  - In `onSubmit`, right after `beginCheckout` and before the window opens: `savePending({ orderRef, rzpOrderId, tier });` (no token, no
    personal data, no amount) and `recovery.dismiss();`. In `startCheckout(...)`: `callbackUrl: prefersRedirectCheckout(navigator.userAgent)
    ? payReturnUrl(window.location.origin) : undefined` (only in-app/WebView browsers get Razorpay's redirect flow, to this host's
    /pay/return; every other browser keeps the window and its handler exactly as before). `clearPending();` in `onDismiss`, in `onPaid`
    (after `clearFormDraft()`), when the window would not open, and in the catch. Nothing else in `onSubmit` moves: the request, the
    amounts, the events, the confirm request (keepalive) and the navigation with the token are as they were.
  - `onContinue` (new): "Continue paying" reopens Razorpay for the SAME order (`recovery.open`: reference, Razorpay order id, key and amount
    from POST /pay/status), prefill from the form's own fields (B3 put them back), the window events and the B7c watch as a normal open
    (not `beginCheckout`: no new checkout started); in a regular browser a payment made in the window confirms with keepalive and goes
    to /thanks through `confirmThenGoToThanks` (the page has no address token: the server sets the cookie on /pay/status); in an in-app
    browser it asks for the redirect flow too. Closing that window again leaves the same notice.
  - JSX: one conditional block above the pay button, `{recovery.open && !busy ? <PayRecoveryNotice onContinue={onContinue}
    onStartAgain={recovery.startAgain} /> : null}`; no existing element, attribute or class changes.
  - The logic signature (checkout-signatures/...PreorderForm.tsx.json) gains exactly: the four import lines (the validate import with
    `normalisePhone`), the `recovery` declaration, `savePending`, `recovery.dismiss()`, the `callbackUrl` property, the four `clearPending();`
    lines, the `onContinue` function, and in `jsx` the conditional and its two handler props; nothing existing is removed or changed.
  - Visible words: three new strings in src/content/en-IN/store/pay-recovery.ts ("Your payment is still open.", "Continue paying", "Start
    again"); no existing string changes.
  - Proof: test/preorder-pay-recovery.test.tsx, test/preorder-pending-payment.test.ts, test/preorder-redirect-checkout.test.ts,
    test/pay-return-route.test.ts, test/pay-status-route.test.ts, test/store-thanks-cleanup.test.tsx (new files); the frozen
    PreorderForm.test.tsx and the JSX contract fixtures are untouched and green.

